Another option with ragged arrays is to change the observation data and associated covariates into long format and use indices for species, site.id <http://site.id>, and the latent state.  I have not compared speeds to know if it is faster.

for (i in 1:n.obs){  # loop over all observations that are in long format
  logit(p[i]) <- lp[species.id <http://species.id>[i]] + beta1[species.id <http://species.id>[i]] * Ju[i] + beta2[species.id <http://species.id>[i]]*Hr[i] + beta3[species.id <http://species.id>[i]]*Rd[i]
  Y[i] ~ dbern(p[i] * z[sited.id <http://sited.id>[i], species.id <http://species.id>[i]])
}

Jesse

